WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.488 --> 00:00:03.800
Your agents forget everything between one

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.128
session and the next.

3
00:00:05.591 --> 00:00:08.394
relembra is a memory that all of them

4
00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:09.382
share:

5
00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:12.063
short facts, chosen by the agent

6
00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:14.571
itself, kept per project.

7
00:00:14.821 --> 00:00:17.523
It is open source, written in TypeScript,

8
00:00:17.543 --> 00:00:20.361
with no runtime dependencies at all.

9
00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:22.964
And it was designed to fit into

10
00:00:22.984 --> 00:00:24.995
any agent system:

11
00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:27.937
the host says who is who, and the core enforces

12
00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:29.028
the rules.

13
00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:34.292
The agent memories that exist today

14
00:00:34.312 --> 00:00:36.814
tend to fall into four traps.

15
00:00:36.872 --> 00:00:37.846
The first:

16
00:00:37.866 --> 00:00:39.834
everything lives in a single stream.

17
00:00:39.854 --> 00:00:43.395
A summary from yesterday mixes four projects

18
00:00:43.415 --> 00:00:45.206
into a single line.

19
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:46.413
The second:

20
00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.175
nothing can be deleted.

21
00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:51.317
A password pasted by mistake stays there

22
00:00:51.337 --> 00:00:52.237
forever.

23
00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:53.135
The third:

24
00:00:53.155 --> 00:00:56.202
they need a server running all the time,

25
00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.345
or they capture every word of the conversation, without

26
00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:00.787
choosing anything.

27
00:01:00.974 --> 00:01:01.739
And the fourth:

28
00:01:01.759 --> 00:01:04.550
they trust search without measuring whether it finds

29
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.354
what agents actually ask.

30
00:01:10.718 --> 00:01:13.423
relembra brings together ideas already proven

31
00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:15.768
in memory systems and in durable

32
00:01:15.788 --> 00:01:16.658
execution.

33
00:01:16.871 --> 00:01:19.585
From curated memory comes the chosen fact:

34
00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:22.456
the agent decides what deserves a line, and

35
00:01:22.476 --> 00:01:25.569
the wake fits in a byte budget.

36
00:01:25.589 --> 00:01:28.471
From durable execution comes the discipline:

37
00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:31.450
write before showing, and repeat an

38
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.679
operation without duplicating it.

39
00:01:33.794 --> 00:01:36.307
From multi-user systems come

40
00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:38.970
a scope on every record and search

41
00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.524
evaluated with numbers.

42
00:01:40.974 --> 00:01:43.108
And it leaves out the mandatory

43
00:01:43.128 --> 00:01:46.097
server, the automatic capture of everything,

44
00:01:46.117 --> 00:01:47.973
and any copied code:

45
00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:50.336
the search algorithm comes from its

46
00:01:50.356 --> 00:01:52.254
own specification.

47
00:01:55.845 --> 00:01:58.902
The principle comes down to six ideas.

48
00:01:58.922 --> 00:01:59.859
Curated.

49
00:01:59.879 --> 00:02:01.295
Scoped.

50
00:02:01.315 --> 00:02:02.491
Bounded.

51
00:02:02.511 --> 00:02:03.568
Durable.

52
00:02:03.588 --> 00:02:04.765
Erasable.

53
00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:06.042
Measured.

54
00:02:06.101 --> 00:02:08.408
It is the combination of all six that the project

55
00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.341
pursues.

56
00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:15.263
At the center, a pure core, with no access to

57
00:02:15.283 --> 00:02:16.625
disk or network:

58
00:02:16.645 --> 00:02:19.805
the event model, the write guard,

59
00:02:19.825 --> 00:02:22.833
BM25 search in Portuguese and English, and the

60
00:02:22.853 --> 00:02:25.045
wake composer.

61
00:02:25.075 --> 00:02:27.621
The core only talks through ports.

62
00:02:27.641 --> 00:02:29.799
Below, the stores:

63
00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:31.743
in memory, for tests;

64
00:02:31.763 --> 00:02:34.776
native SQLite, which runs on Node and

65
00:02:34.796 --> 00:02:35.165
Bun;

66
00:02:35.185 --> 00:02:38.431
and Postgres, which shares one memory

67
00:02:38.451 --> 00:02:39.995
across machines.

68
00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.054
Every store goes through the same

69
00:02:43.074 --> 00:02:44.870
conformance suite.

70
00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.992
Anyone who writes a new adapter proves, with

71
00:02:48.012 --> 00:02:50.752
the same tests, that it behaves

72
00:02:50.772 --> 00:02:51.580
the same.

73
00:02:51.741 --> 00:02:53.669
On top, the integrations:

74
00:02:53.689 --> 00:02:56.863
the command line, the session-start

75
00:02:56.883 --> 00:03:00.135
hooks, the MCP server and pi-durable,

76
00:03:00.155 --> 00:03:02.091
the default integration.

77
00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.653
The command line is a single binary

78
00:03:05.673 --> 00:03:07.401
compiled with Bun.

79
00:03:07.421 --> 00:03:10.814
The library runs on Bun and on Node 24 or

80
00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.050
newer.

81
00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:16.252
Follow one memory from start to finish.

82
00:03:16.356 --> 00:03:18.375
The agent writes a line.

83
00:03:18.395 --> 00:03:21.507
The guard refuses more than 280 bytes, line

84
00:03:21.527 --> 00:03:24.638
breaks, invisible characters and known

85
00:03:24.658 --> 00:03:27.333
credential formats, without ever

86
00:03:27.353 --> 00:03:29.546
repeating the refused text.

87
00:03:29.689 --> 00:03:32.145
Every write carries an operation

88
00:03:32.165 --> 00:03:33.382
identity (op id).

89
00:03:33.402 --> 00:03:35.996
If the call is repeated after a

90
00:03:36.016 --> 00:03:38.884
crash, the stored result comes back, and nothing

91
00:03:38.904 --> 00:03:40.029
is duplicated.

92
00:03:40.458 --> 00:03:43.297
In the same transaction, the host can check

93
00:03:43.317 --> 00:03:45.947
whether the writer still holds authority.

94
00:03:45.967 --> 00:03:48.667
A late write, after losing

95
00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:51.288
that authority, records nothing.

96
00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.808
In the next session, the wake respects

97
00:03:54.828 --> 00:03:57.294
a default limit of 9,500 bytes:

98
00:03:57.314 --> 00:04:00.307
first the pinned memories, then the

99
00:04:00.327 --> 00:04:03.471
project's recent ones, then the summaries, and

100
00:04:03.491 --> 00:04:05.900
finally an index of the rest.

101
00:04:06.099 --> 00:04:08.928
And each memory reaches the model as

102
00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:11.857
attributed evidence, with identity,

103
00:04:11.877 --> 00:04:13.282
scope and revision.

104
00:04:13.302 --> 00:04:16.527
A fact to weigh, never an order to

105
00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:17.559
follow.

106
00:04:19.432 --> 00:04:22.398
relembra does not know who the user is.

107
00:04:22.418 --> 00:04:23.969
The host does:

108
00:04:23.989 --> 00:04:27.348
Project A, Project B, every system that

109
00:04:27.368 --> 00:04:28.532
integrates it.

110
00:04:28.662 --> 00:04:31.127
Each host provides a policy:

111
00:04:31.147 --> 00:04:34.155
from its own login, it says

112
00:04:34.175 --> 00:04:37.339
which scopes that principal may read,

113
00:04:37.359 --> 00:04:38.970
write and promote.

114
00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:41.921
Project A can separate by user;

115
00:04:41.941 --> 00:04:44.182
Project B, by team.

116
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.021
The scope never comes from what the model

117
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:47.658
typed.

118
00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:50.210
And the filter applies before the search:

119
00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.974
whatever is out of scope never even enters

120
00:04:52.994 --> 00:04:53.770
the count.

121
00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.688
On the command line, every session also reads

122
00:04:56.708 --> 00:04:59.606
a global scope, with rules for all

123
00:04:59.626 --> 00:05:02.049
projects, but only writes to its own

124
00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:02.980
project.

125
00:05:03.021 --> 00:05:06.248
With pi-durable, the operation identity

126
00:05:06.268 --> 00:05:09.268
combines the conversation, the task and the call.

127
00:05:09.288 --> 00:05:12.137
If the process crashes after writing and

128
00:05:12.157 --> 00:05:15.308
before confirming, the retry returns the

129
00:05:15.328 --> 00:05:16.761
same memory.

130
00:05:16.867 --> 00:05:19.510
And an egress filter, also the host's,

131
00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.384
masks or blocks what each principal

132
00:05:22.404 --> 00:05:25.227
may see, right before the text leaves.

133
00:05:27.123 --> 00:05:29.433
Deleting has to be real.

134
00:05:29.687 --> 00:05:32.216
Retracting hides a memory from agents,

135
00:05:32.236 --> 00:05:34.587
but the owner can still review it.

136
00:05:34.815 --> 00:05:37.469
Redacting swaps the text for a tombstone and

137
00:05:37.489 --> 00:05:40.424
invalidates, in the same transaction, every summary

138
00:05:40.444 --> 00:05:42.081
that depended on it.

139
00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:45.379
Every egress records which memories it took

140
00:05:45.399 --> 00:05:47.001
out of relembra.

141
00:05:47.021 --> 00:05:49.894
After one is redacted, relembra hands

142
00:05:49.914 --> 00:05:52.856
the host each destination that received the text,

143
00:05:52.876 --> 00:05:55.466
until it hears acknowledged or unsupported.

144
00:05:55.486 --> 00:05:58.537
And it never says a copy was erased.

145
00:05:58.917 --> 00:06:01.814
And a per-scope retention rule redacts

146
00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.803
expired memories when the host runs the

147
00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:05.585
sweep.

148
00:06:05.605 --> 00:06:08.218
Removing the copies outside relembra is

149
00:06:08.238 --> 00:06:11.277
the host's job, and the project says so

150
00:06:11.297 --> 00:06:12.807
in plain words.

151
00:06:16.353 --> 00:06:19.487
And none of this is accepted on preference.

152
00:06:19.507 --> 00:06:21.343
First, it is measured.

153
00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:24.172
An evaluator asks the same questions of

154
00:06:24.192 --> 00:06:26.883
relembra and of 17 control candidates,

155
00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:29.730
built to fail, and counts hits among

156
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.509
the first five (hit@5), the rank of the

157
00:06:32.529 --> 00:06:35.355
hit (MRR), and when the right answer is

158
00:06:35.375 --> 00:06:36.421
not knowing.

159
00:06:36.865 --> 00:06:38.624
It also counts leaks:

160
00:06:38.644 --> 00:06:41.115
a denied scope, a deleted memory that

161
00:06:41.135 --> 00:06:44.033
reappears, even an identity left loose in an

162
00:06:44.053 --> 00:06:45.050
answer.

163
00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.866
Malformed answers are refused, and

164
00:06:47.886 --> 00:06:49.888
whoever hangs loses on time.

165
00:06:49.908 --> 00:06:53.240
A candidate cannot game the score.

166
00:06:53.275 --> 00:06:56.647
And speed is measured over 20,000

167
00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:57.563
memories.

168
00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:01.047
With the process already running, 95% of searches

169
00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:04.255
finish in under 10 ms on Bun.

170
00:07:04.275 --> 00:07:07.325
On Node, in just over 40.

171
00:07:09.685 --> 00:07:12.293
relembra grows in layers, each one

172
00:07:12.313 --> 00:07:14.905
on top of a product that already works.

173
00:07:15.326 --> 00:07:18.971
v0.1 runs on one machine, with SQLite.

174
00:07:18.991 --> 00:07:22.733
v0.2 shares across machines through

175
00:07:22.753 --> 00:07:25.626
Postgres and turns on pi-durable.

176
00:07:25.646 --> 00:07:29.388
v0.3 brings the MCP server, promotion

177
00:07:29.408 --> 00:07:33.438
across scopes and the release gates.

178
00:07:33.458 --> 00:07:37.586
Today, version 0.3.0 is a private preview:

179
00:07:37.606 --> 00:07:41.154
the code is MIT, and the repository opens

180
00:07:41.174 --> 00:07:42.246
later.

181
00:07:42.505 --> 00:07:45.556
Five years from now, models and vendors

182
00:07:45.576 --> 00:07:46.556
will have changed.

183
00:07:46.576 --> 00:07:49.199
Memory has to outlive them:

184
00:07:49.219 --> 00:07:52.055
an open, documented format, scope

185
00:07:52.075 --> 00:07:54.984
from the very first event, and an evaluation

186
00:07:55.004 --> 00:07:57.356
that grows with every real error.

187
00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:58.137
relembra.

188
00:07:58.157 --> 00:08:01.262
One memory for all your agents.

189
00:08:01.282 --> 00:08:03.926
Measured before it is trusted.
